    "https://www.usf.edu/work-at-usf/careers/benefits.aspx": {
      "title": "Benefits and Perks",
      "description": "Benefits and Perks Skip to Main Content University of South Florida - 70 Est. 1956 University of South Florida - 70 Est. 1956 Search Search USF: Work at USF Central Human Resources Quick Links Recruitment Home Student Employment USF State Retiree Reemployment Applicant Toolkit Regulatory Information Benefits and Perks Contact Recruitment Accepted an Offer - Next Steps How to Apply Applicant Toolkit Accepted an Offer? Quick Links Visit USF Parking Permits Activate USF NetID Fall Academic Calendar BullTracker® USF Athletics Student Tickets St. Petersburg Campus USF Health Give Search MyUSF Apply Quick Links Visit USF Parking Permits Activate USF NetID Fall Academic Calendar BullTracker® USF Athletics Student Tickets St. Petersburg Campus USF Health Give Search Search USF: MyUSF Apply Work at USF Central Human Resources Quick Links Recruitment Home Student Employment USF State Retiree Reemployment Applicant Toolkit Regulatory Information Benefits and Perks Contact Recruitment Accepted an Offer - Next Steps How to Apply Applicant Toolkit Accepted an Offer? Benefits and Perks Breadcrumb Navigation Work at USF Careers Benefits and Perks USF offers a competitive total package. Try the total compensation calculator to see what the complete value of your compensation package may look like. This page provides an at-a-glance view of benefits. Please review the Benefits Summary for more details about the benefits you can participate in as an employee with USF. Insurance Faculty, Administrative and Staff Below are types of insurance programs available to employees appointed to regular\n                                    Faculty, Administration, or Staff positions: Health, Dental and Vision Insurance Plans State Life and Optional Life Insurance Plans Supplemental Insurance Plans such as Cancer, Hospitalization, Intensive Care, and\n                                       Accident/Disability Medical and Dependent Care Flexible Reimbursement Account Domestic Partner Health Insurance Stipend Long-term Disability Insurance Long-term Care Insurance Postdoctoral Scholars Employees appointed to a Postdoctoral Scholar position are offered two different benefit\n                                    program options. Postdoctoral Scholars are allowed to participate in some of the same\n                                    State sponsored insurance programs offered to Faculty, Administration, and Staff if\n                                    they are appointed to work 30 hours or more per week. In addition, Postdoctoral Scholars\n                                    are offered University sponsored insurance plans: STATE SPONSORED INSURANCE PROGRAMS Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Plans State Life Insurance Supplemental Insurance Plans such as Cancer, Hospitalization, Intensive Care and Accident/Disability Dependent Care Flexible Reimbursement Account UNIVERSITY SPONSORED INSURANCE PROGRAMS University Sponsored Health and Dental Insurance Plans Long-term Disability Insurance Long-term Care Insurance Additional Life Insurance Graduate Assistants Most employees appointed to a Graduate Assistantship position are offered a student\n                                    health insurance, which is paid by USF. The insurance plan is provided by the University\n                                    Student Health Insurance office. Temporary Employees Employees appointed in a temporary position working 30 hours or more may be offered\n                                    the below insurance plans. The 30 work hours can be a combination of hours worked\n                                    at USF and another State Agency. Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance Plans State Life Insurance Supplemental Insurance Plans such as Cancer, Hospitalization, Intensive Care, and\n                                       Accident/Disability Dependent Care Flexible Reimbursement Account Long-term Disability Insurance Long-term Care Insurance Additional Life Insurance . Retirement The University of South Florida provides employees the opportunity to participate\n                              in several different retirement and savings programs. All regular Faculty, Administration,\n                              and Staff employees are required to participate in a retirement plan sponsored by\n                              the State of Florida. For our part-time, seasonal and temporary employees not covered by the Florida Retirement\n                              System, the University of South Florida offers a qualified 401(a) – FICA Alternative\n                              retirement plan. Eligible employees are automatically enrolled in this Temporary Employee\n                              Retirement Plan (TERP) upon employment. Additionally, all Employees can participate in the voluntary retirement savings plans\n                              offered by the University of South Florida. 403(b) Tax Sheltered Annuities and 457\n                              State Deferred Compensation plans offer employees the opportunity to save money for\n                              retirement while reducing their current income tax liability. Employees who take a distribution/rollover or receive a benefit from their State of\n                              Florida retirement plan at the time of termination are considered retirees from the\n                              University or State. Retirees seeking re-employment should consider the impact of\n                              any re-employment. View more information about retiree re-employment. Holidays Faculty, Administration and Staff employees enjoy nine paid holidays as listed below.\n                              While most offices will close, there will be exceptions due to the nature of work\n                              performed. In addition, the University President may announce additional floating\n                              holidays. Although most Temporary employees are not eligible to be paid for these days off,\n                              the following temporary employee groups are paid for holidays: Professional, salaried temporary Salaried graduate assistants/associates covered by the collective bargaining agreementAdjunct\n                                 faculty who are working their regularly required work schedule Regular staff employees who have successfully completed their probationary period\n                                 are eligible for one personal holiday each year in addition to the holidays listed\n                                 below: PAID HOLIDAYS New Year's Day Martin Luther King, Jr. Day Memorial Day Junteenth Independence Day Labor Day Veteran's Day Thanksgiving Day Day after Thanksgiving Christmas Day Tuition-Related Benefits EMPLOYEE TUITION PROGRAM Employees are encouraged to pursue continuous learning and USF waives tuition costs\n                              for up to 6 credit hours per semester for employees that meet the program eligibility\n                              requirements. Learn more here about the Employee Tuition Program here. DEPENDENT TUITION REMISSION PROGRAM The Dependent Tuition Remission Program covers in-state tuition for eligible undergraduate\n                              courses for the employee’s spouse/domestic partner or dependent child. Learn more\n                              about the Dependent Tuition Remission Program here. PUBLIC SERVICE LOAN FORGIVENESS If you are employed by a government or not-for-profit organization, you may be eligible\n                              to receive loan forgiveness under the Public Service Loan Forgiveness Program. Learn\n                              more about Public Service Loan Forgiveness here. PAYROLL DEDUCTION FOR FLORIDA PREPAID COLLEGE PLANS USF employees can payroll deduct their Florida Prepaid College Plan expenses. Learn\n                              more about payroll deduction for Florida prepaid college plans here. Learning Opportunities USF offers its employees opportunities for both personal and professional learning\n                              and development. FREE EMPLOYEE ACCESS TO LINKEDIN LEARNING Build, refine and add new skills with access to over 16,000 online courses. HR  TALENT DEVELOPMENT USF employees can also benefit from internal training offered by the Talent Development\n                              team (TD). TD offers professional development for supervisors and managers, team development\n                              and organization development through the Employee Success Center. INNOVATIVE EDUCATION Innovative Education on the Tampa campus provides employees with many learning opportunities - Graduate\n                              Certificates, Professional Development Opportunities, Testing Services, as well as\n                              Programs for Seniors (50+). Many of the programs are offered fully or partially online.\n                              Employees can receive discounts on select offerings from Innvoative Education through\n                              the Employee Success Center. USF LIBRARIES Employees have access to a wealth of services at the USF Libraries. Tampa Campus Sarasota/Manatee Campus St. Petersburg Campus Employee Recognition At the University of South Florida we recognize that our employees make a difference\n                              in our success. We take every opportunity to celebrate their contributions and thank\n                              them for their service in a variety of ways: LENGTH OF SERVICE USF's Length of Service Recognition program celebrates the long term commitment of\n                              our unBullievable employees to the University. FACULTY AWARDS Numerous University awards include University Distinguished Professor, Emeritus Professor,\n                              Outstanding Undergraduate Teaching & Advising awards and Outstanding Community-Engaged\n                              Teaching Awards. Additionally, USF is proud to recognize the numerous external awards earned by our faculty. OUTSTANDING STAFF AWARDS The Outstanding Staff Awards recognize employees who exemplify excellence through\n                              their daily commitment to the University. QUIET QUALITY AWARDS The Quiet Quality Awards were implemented by the Staff Senate with strong support\n                              from USF administration in a collaborative effort to increase employee recognition. Work/Life Balance USF offers a wide variety of programs, events, conveniences and amenities in a beautiful\n                              and welcoming environment providing opportunities to help balance work and life demands. CHILDCARE ON CAMPUS USF Preschool for Creative Learning FLORIDA PREPAID COLLEGE PLANS USF accommodates employees who participate in a Florida Prepaid College Plan by offering\n                              payroll deduction. USF CAMPUS RECREATION USF Campus Recreation offers membership to USF employees. This is a state of the art facility with programs\n                              that include Aquatics, Fitness, Intra-murals, Outdoor Recreation and Sports Clubs\n                              and is conveniently located on the Tampa campus. EMPLOYEE ASSISTANCE PROGRAM The University of South Florida's Employee Assistance Program (EAP) is a service program\n                              designed to assist employees with personal, family, or workplace concerns/issues. Campus Resources USF offers a wide variety of on-campus resources, such as: TAMPA CAMPUS Arts and Culture: See College of the Arts Event Calendar here with many FREE Admission opportunities! Athletics and Fitness Dining on Campus Services on Campus USF Federal Credit Union Pharmacies: For the convenience of USF employees the Bulls Country Pharmacy in the\n                                 Marshall Student Center and the Morsani Center Pharmacy are located on the Tampa Campus. ST. PETE CAMPUS Campus Resources Campus Recreation SARASOTA/MANATEE CAMPUS Campus Life Fitness Center Campus Cafe Discounts & Perks Faculty and staff can receive various discounts for goods, services and recreation.\n                              Our Discounts & Perks list is continually updated. University of South Florida Located in Tampa and St. Petersburg. 4202 E. Fowler Avenue Tampa, FL 33612, USA 813-974-2970 About USF Academics Admissions Locations Campus Life Research Administrative Units Regulations & Policies Human Resources Work at USF Emergency & Safety Title IX USF Health USF Athletics USF Alumni Support USF USF Libraries USF World Copyright © 2026, University of South Florida. All rights reserved. This website is maintained by Human Resources . About This Site Contact USF Visit USF Accessibility"
    },
    "https://www.usf.edu/work-at-usf/careers/student-employment.aspx": {
      "title": "Student Employment",
      "description": "Student Employment Skip to Main Content University of South Florida - 70 Est. 1956 University of South Florida - 70 Est. 1956 Search Search USF: Work at USF Central Human Resources Quick Links Recruitment Home Student Employment USF State Retiree Reemployment Applicant Toolkit Regulatory Information Benefits and Perks Contact Recruitment Accepted an Offer - Next Steps How to Apply Applicant Toolkit Accepted an Offer? Quick Links Visit USF Parking Permits Activate USF NetID Fall Academic Calendar BullTracker® USF Athletics Student Tickets St. Petersburg Campus USF Health Give Search MyUSF Apply Quick Links Visit USF Parking Permits Activate USF NetID Fall Academic Calendar BullTracker® USF Athletics Student Tickets St. Petersburg Campus USF Health Give Search Search USF: MyUSF Apply Work at USF Central Human Resources Quick Links Recruitment Home Student Employment USF State Retiree Reemployment Applicant Toolkit Regulatory Information Benefits and Perks Contact Recruitment Accepted an Offer - Next Steps How to Apply Applicant Toolkit Accepted an Offer? Student Employment Breadcrumb Navigation Work at USF Careers Student Employment Getting Started The Center for Career & Professional Development operates as part of Student Success. This center is separate from Central Human Resources\n                  and offers special services for USF students including career planning, assessments,\n                  mock interviews, resume and cover letter assistance and more. Find information about the Federal Work Study program here. Browse Job Openings APPLY FOR ON-CAMPUS AND OFF-CAMPUS JOBS ON HANDSHAKE The Center for Career & Professional Development uses Handshake, an on-line career\n                  management and job search system for USF students looking for internships, part-time,\n                  and full-time employment opportunities. Learn more about how Handshake works here. Access Handshake Learn more about Internships and Co-ops. Information for International Students Generally, F-1 students are only allowed to work on campus for 20 hours per week during\n                        the Fall and Spring semesters (40 hours during breaks and annual vacation). For a\n                        job to be considered to be “on campus” you must receive a USF generated paycheck or\n                        the on-campus location must offer essential services to students, such as the Yuengling\n                        Center or the USF Follett Bookstore. Types of Employment Optional Practical Training INCREASE WORK HOURS DURING BREAKS & VACATIONS Employment must not exceed 20 hours a week while school is in session, but an F-1\n                        student may work on campus full-time when school is not in session or during annual\n                        vacation. UNITED STATES INCOME TAX Your paycheck may be lower than the anticipated amount due to tax withholdings. The\n                        amount withheld from your paycheck is dependent upon your tax status which, in turn,\n                        is determined by your visa classification and the amount of time you have been in\n                        the United States. Access further tax information here. About Your Paycheck The University of South Florida pays on a bi-weekly payroll cycle. Each pay period\n                  begins on Friday and ends two weeks later on Thursday. You will be paid for that pay\n                  period one week later on Friday. Learn more about your paycheck and student FICA guidelines here. Access a student Cost Calculator here. University of South Florida Located in Tampa and St. Petersburg. 4202 E. Fowler Avenue Tampa, FL 33612, USA 813-974-2970 About USF Academics Admissions Locations Campus Life Research Administrative Units Regulations & Policies Human Resources Work at USF Emergency & Safety Title IX USF Health USF Athletics USF Alumni Support USF USF Libraries USF World Copyright © 2026, University of South Florida. All rights reserved. This website is maintained by Human Resources . About This Site Contact USF Visit USF Accessibility"
    },
    "https://www.usf.edu/work-at-usf/careers/stories-usf-health.aspx": {
      "title": "USF Health:  Making Life Better",
      "description": "USF Health:  Making Life Better | Careers@USF | University of South Florida Skip to Main Content University of South Florida - 70 Est. 1956 University of South Florida - 70 Est. 1956 Search Search USF: Work at USF Central Human Resources Quick Links Recruitment Home Student Employment USF State Retiree Reemployment Applicant Toolkit Regulatory Information Benefits and Perks Contact Recruitment Accepted an Offer - Next Steps How to Apply Applicant Toolkit Accepted an Offer? Quick Links Visit USF Parking Permits Activate USF NetID Fall Academic Calendar BullTracker® USF Athletics Student Tickets St. Petersburg Campus USF Health Give Search MyUSF Apply Quick Links Visit USF Parking Permits Activate USF NetID Fall Academic Calendar BullTracker® USF Athletics Student Tickets St. Petersburg Campus USF Health Give Search Search USF: MyUSF Apply Work at USF Central Human Resources Quick Links Recruitment Home Student Employment USF State Retiree Reemployment Applicant Toolkit Regulatory Information Benefits and Perks Contact Recruitment Accepted an Offer - Next Steps How to Apply Applicant Toolkit Accepted an Offer? USF Health:  Making Life Better Our employees are the engine driving healthcare change forward at USF Health. It’s\n                        their commitment to the kindest care for patients, the most inspiring education for\n                        students, and the most innovative breakthroughs in research that make USF Health a\n                        force for positive change. Breadcrumb Navigation Work at USF Careers USF Health:  Making Life Better See the stories for yourself. As an academic medical center, USF Health delivers the highest quality service with\n                  the most innovative technologies, providing resources few other physicians groups\n                  can offer – all this while leading the way in life-changing research and training\n                  the next generation of medical professionals.  To explore job opportunities at USF Health, click here. Jessica was diagnosed with severe endometriosis, which caused several years of infertility\n                     and relentless pain. Julio  suffered 2 heart attacks over 7 years. After two procedures elsewhere, he was\n                     faced with a third and an uncertain future. Greg, a professional artist, could no longer paint due to a brain tumor. Ashley's unborn twins were sharing a common monochorionic placenta and receiving an\n                     unequal amount of blood volume. After suffering from failed surgeries and painful arthritis, grateful patient Ellen\n                     Polack has regained the use of her hands, pain free. Al and Betty were college sweethearts who travled the world. After being married for\n                     68 years, Betty started having memory loss. University of South Florida Located in Tampa and St. Petersburg. 4202 E. Fowler Avenue Tampa, FL 33612, USA 813-974-2970 About USF Academics Admissions Locations Campus Life Research Administrative Units Regulations & Policies Human Resources Work at USF Emergency & Safety Title IX USF Health USF Athletics USF Alumni Support USF USF Libraries USF World Copyright © 2026, University of South Florida. All rights reserved. This website is maintained by Human Resources . About This Site Contact USF Visit USF Accessibility"
    },
    "https://www.usf.edu/work-at-usf/careers/regulatory-information.aspx": {
      "title": "Regulatory Information",
      "description": "Regulatory Information Skip to Main Content University of South Florida - 70 Est. 1956 University of South Florida - 70 Est. 1956 Search Search USF: Work at USF Central Human Resources Quick Links Recruitment Home Student Employment USF State Retiree Reemployment Applicant Toolkit Regulatory Information Benefits and Perks Contact Recruitment Accepted an Offer - Next Steps How to Apply Applicant Toolkit Accepted an Offer? Quick Links Visit USF Parking Permits Activate USF NetID Fall Academic Calendar BullTracker® USF Athletics Student Tickets St. Petersburg Campus USF Health Give Search MyUSF Apply Quick Links Visit USF Parking Permits Activate USF NetID Fall Academic Calendar BullTracker® USF Athletics Student Tickets St. Petersburg Campus USF Health Give Search Search USF: MyUSF Apply Work at USF Central Human Resources Quick Links Recruitment Home Student Employment USF State Retiree Reemployment Applicant Toolkit Regulatory Information Benefits and Perks Contact Recruitment Accepted an Offer - Next Steps How to Apply Applicant Toolkit Accepted an Offer? Regulatory Information Breadcrumb Navigation Work at USF Careers Regulatory Information Veterans' Preference In compliance with Florida Statute 295, USF is committed to providing preference to\n                  U.S. veterans and their spouses in the hire, promotion, and retention of all Staff\n                  (Non-Exempt) level positions. Veterans' Preference is extended to those who fall under\n                  the specified categories. Specified Categories Eligibility Requirements Determining Veteran's Preference Title IX Pursuant to Title IX, the University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in\n                  educational programs or activities that it operates. Such protection extends to applicants,\n                  employees, and students. Any questions or inquiries concerning to the application\n                  of Title IX may be referred to the Title IX Coordinator, or to any of the University's\n                  Title IX Deputy Coordinators. The most up-to-date information on the University's\n                  Title IX Coordinator and Deputy Coordinators can be found on the Title IX website. More About Title IX: What is it? USF Policy 0-004 Veteran Status/Disability (VEVRAA/503) To self-disclose Veteran Status and/or a Disability you must first activate your USF\n                  Net ID, then log into GEMS Self-Service, under Personal Information, choose either\n                  Veteran Status and/or Disability. Please note that this does NOT address the need\n                  for an accommodation under the ADA. For an ADA accommodation, review the policy and\n                  procedure. Activate Net ID USF Policy 0-108 (ADA) ADA Accommodation Procedure Background and Criminal Records Checks The University of South Florida is committed to protecting the safety, security and\n                  health of its students, employees and others. USF requires that a criminal history\n                  background check be conducted on prospective employees as a condition of employment.\n                  Criminal background checks may be required for students or volunteers depending upon\n                  assignment. Background Check Information Security Policy & Criminal Stats - Cleary Act Schools must publish an annual report disclosing campus security policy, three years'\n                  worth of selected crime statistics, and make timely warnings about crimes that pose\n                  an ongoing threat to students and employees. Under the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of\n                  Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, Campus Security Authorities\n                  play a vital role in the timely and accurate reporting of certain crimes and incidents\n                  within USF. Security Report and Safety Guide Campus Security Authority Your Safety Federal Employment Laws Applicants also have rights under Federal Employment Laws: Family and Medical Leave Act (FMLA) and Employee Polygraph Protection Act (EPPA) . University of South Florida Located in Tampa and St. Petersburg. 4202 E. Fowler Avenue Tampa, FL 33612, USA 813-974-2970 About USF Academics Admissions Locations Campus Life Research Administrative Units Regulations & Policies Human Resources Work at USF Emergency & Safety Title IX USF Health USF Athletics USF Alumni Support USF USF Libraries USF World Copyright © 2026, University of South Florida. All rights reserved. This website is maintained by Human Resources . About This Site Contact USF Visit USF Accessibility"
    },
    "https://www.usf.edu/work-at-usf/careers/usf-state-retiree-employment.aspx": {
      "title": "USF/State Retiree Reemployment",
      "description": "USF/State Retiree Reemployment Skip to Main Content University of South Florida - 70 Est. 1956 University of South Florida - 70 Est. 1956 Search Search USF: Work at USF Central Human Resources Quick Links Recruitment Home Student Employment USF State Retiree Reemployment Applicant Toolkit Regulatory Information Benefits and Perks Contact Recruitment Accepted an Offer - Next Steps How to Apply Applicant Toolkit Accepted an Offer? Quick Links Visit USF Parking Permits Activate USF NetID Fall Academic Calendar BullTracker® USF Athletics Student Tickets St. Petersburg Campus USF Health Give Search MyUSF Apply Quick Links Visit USF Parking Permits Activate USF NetID Fall Academic Calendar BullTracker® USF Athletics Student Tickets St. Petersburg Campus USF Health Give Search Search USF: MyUSF Apply Work at USF Central Human Resources Quick Links Recruitment Home Student Employment USF State Retiree Reemployment Applicant Toolkit Regulatory Information Benefits and Perks Contact Recruitment Accepted an Offer - Next Steps How to Apply Applicant Toolkit Accepted an Offer? USF/State Retiree Reemployment Breadcrumb Navigation Work at USF Careers USF/State Retiree Reemployment If you are receiving a benefit under the FRS pension plan or have taken a withdrawal,\n                  including a rollover, from another state-administered retirement plan, such as the\n                  FRS Investment Plan, the State University System Optional Retirement Program (SUSORP),\n                  the Senior Management Service Optional Annuity Program (SMSOAP), or the State Community\n                  College System Optional Retirement Program (SCCSORP), you may be under restrictions\n                  for reemployment. Reemployment prior to completing the required termination period may result in suspension\n                     or loss of your benefits. It is an applicant’s responsibility to follow the FRS requirements when applying for\n                     reemployment. These definitions and restrictions are from the Department of Management Services\n                  webpage in the Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ) document on Retirement. You are considered \"retired\" from the Florida Retirement System (FRS) if: You have received any benefits under the FRS Pension Plan (including DROP), or You have taken any distribution (including a rollover) from the FRS Investment Plan,\n                     or alternative retirement programs offered by state universities (SUSORP), state community\n                     colleges (SCCORP), state government for senior managers (SMSOAP), or local governments\n                     for senior managers. These restrictions are especially critical for DROP participants, as returning to\n                  work too soon could result in having to repay and forfeit the large lump-sum DROP\n                  payout. If you retire and wish to come back to work here at USF, please contact the\n                  Human Resources office prior to signing any employment paperwork. FRS Pension Plan retirees remain ineligible for renewed membership and will not earn\n                  any additional State Retirement benefits if initially reemployed on or after July\n                  1, 2010. If you are a retiree of SUSORP, the FRS Investment Plan, the Senior Management\n                  Service Optional Annuity Program (SMSOAP), or the State Community College System Optional\n                  Retirement Program (SCCSORP), you will become a renewed member of the FRS Investment\n                  Plan or the SUSORP, depending upon the plan covering the position when you are employed\n                  in a regularly established position and you are initially enrolled on or after July\n                  1, 2017. Please review the Department of Management Services FAQ document on Retirement for important information before applying and/or accepting a new offer of employment\n                  from USF. HR has developed this digital guide to help retirees in the important and exciting\n                     journey through retirement. You'll find guidance on what you can and can't do as a USF/State retired employee.\n                  Please click here for a GUIDE to YOUR SUCCESSFUL RETIREMENT! University of South Florida Located in Tampa and St. Petersburg. 4202 E. Fowler Avenue Tampa, FL 33612, USA 813-974-2970 About USF Academics Admissions Locations Campus Life Research Administrative Units Regulations & Policies Human Resources Work at USF Emergency & Safety Title IX USF Health USF Athletics USF Alumni Support USF USF Libraries USF World Copyright © 2026, University of South Florida. All rights reserved. This website is maintained by Human Resources . About This Site Contact USF Visit USF Accessibility"
    },
    "https://www.usf.edu/work-at-usf/careers/contact.aspx": {
      "title": "Contact Recruiting",
